{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This snippet shows the three core Lit Query concepts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/queries.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queries"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/mutations.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutations"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/query-invalidation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Invalidation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For complete runnable examples, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/pagination","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  QueryClientProvider,\n  createMutationController,\n  createQueryController,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { addTodo, getTodos } from './api'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: getTodos,\n  })\n\n  private readonly createTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: async () => {\n      await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    const mutation = this.createTodo()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      <ul>\n        ${query.data.map((todo) => html`<li>${todo.title}</li>`)}\n      </ul>\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${mutation.isPending}\n        @click=${() => this.createTodo.mutate({ title: 'Write Lit docs' })}\n      >\n        Add Todo\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('todos-view', TodosView)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mount the provider around your component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The controllers are created with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" because a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitElement"},{"type":"text","value":" is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactiveControllerHost"},{"type":"text","value":". Lit Query uses the host lifecycle to subscribe, request updates, and clean up when the element disconnects."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Continue with "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/reactive-controllers-vs-hooks.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive Controllers vs Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if you know React Query, or go straight to "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/queries.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis snippet shows the three core Lit Query concepts:\n\n- [Queries](./guides/queries.md)\n- [Mutations](./guides/mutations.md)\n- [Query Invalidation](./guides/query-invalidation.md)\n\nFor complete runnable examples, see [Basic](./examples/basic), [Pagination](./examples/pagination), and [SSR](./examples/ssr).\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  QueryClientProvider,\n  createMutationController,\n  createQueryController,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { addTodo, getTodos } from './api'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: getTodos,\n  })\n\n  private readonly createTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: async () => {\n      await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    const mutation = this.createTodo()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      <ul>\n        ${query.data.map((todo) => html`<li>${todo.title}</li>`)}\n      </ul>\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${mutation.isPending}\n        @click=${() => this.createTodo.mutate({ title: 'Write Lit docs' })}\n      >\n        Add Todo\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('todos-view', TodosView)\n```\n\nMount the provider around your component:\n\n```html\n<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>\n```\n\nThe controllers are created with `this` because a `LitElement` is a `ReactiveControllerHost`. Lit Query uses the host lifecycle to subscribe, request updates, and clean up when the element disconnects.\n\nContinue with [Reactive Controllers vs Hooks](./guides/reactive-controllers-vs-hooks.md) if you know React Query, or go straight to [Queries](./guides/queries.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: quick-start\ntitle: Quick Start\n---\n\nThis snippet shows the three core Lit Query concepts:\n\n- [Queries](./guides/queries.md)\n- [Mutations](./guides/mutations.md)\n- [Query Invalidation](./guides/query-invalidation.md)\n\nFor complete runnable examples, see [Basic](./examples/basic), [Pagination](./examples/pagination), and [SSR](./examples/ssr).\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement, html } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  QueryClientProvider,\n  createMutationController,\n  createQueryController,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\nimport { addTodo, getTodos } from './api'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass AppQueryProvider extends QueryClientProvider {\n  constructor() {\n    super()\n    this.client = queryClient\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('app-query-provider', AppQueryProvider)\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: getTodos,\n  })\n\n  private readonly createTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n    onSuccess: async () => {\n      await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n    },\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    const mutation = this.createTodo()\n\n    if (query.isPending) return html`Loading...`\n    if (query.isError) return html`Error: ${query.error.message}`\n\n    return html`\n      <ul>\n        ${query.data.map((todo) => html`<li>${todo.title}</li>`)}\n      </ul>\n\n      <button\n        ?disabled=${mutation.isPending}\n        @click=${() => this.createTodo.mutate({ title: 'Write Lit docs' })}\n      >\n        Add Todo\n      </button>\n    `\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define('todos-view', TodosView)\n```\n\nMount the provider around your component:\n\n```html\n<app-query-provider>\n  <todos-view></todos-view>\n</app-query-provider>\n```\n\nThe controllers are created with `this` because a `LitElement` is a `ReactiveControllerHost`. Lit Query uses the host lifecycle to subscribe, request updates, and clean up when the element disconnects.\n\nContinue with [Reactive Controllers vs Hooks](./guides/reactive-controllers-vs-hooks.md) if you know React Query, or go straight to [Queries](./guides/queries.md).\n"}
